# Releasing {{.Name}}

This project publishes to the personal Homebrew tap via `jwa-tobrew` (kind: **{{.Kind}}**). The full system is documented at <https://github.com/jwa91/homebrew-tap>.

## TL;DR

```bash
{{if eq .Kind "go"}}git tag -a v<version> -m v<version> && git push origin v<version>
op run --env-file=.env.template -- goreleaser release --clean{{else}}op run --env-file=.env.template -- ./scripts/release.sh <version> <path/to/artifact>{{end}}
```

After it completes, the new version is installable as `brew install jwa91/tap/{{.Name}}`.

## Preconditions

- Working tree is clean (`git status`)
- Version is a semver string without the `v` prefix (the script tags `vX.Y.Z`)
- `gh`, `git`{{if eq .Kind "go"}}, `goreleaser`{{end}}, `op`, and `jwa-tobrew` are on PATH
- 1Password CLI is signed in (`op whoami`)

## What the wrapper does

`op run --env-file=.env.template` resolves the `op://` references in `.env.template` and exports the resolved secrets to the child process for the duration of the command. Nothing is written to disk; the secrets exist only in that process tree. Never `export` these tokens to a long-lived shell.

{{if eq .Kind "go"}}For Go projects, GoReleaser is the entire release pipeline (same command runs locally and in CI). It:

1. Verifies HEAD is tagged with the version you intend to release
2. Builds cross-platform binaries (darwin+linux, amd64+arm64)
3. Creates a GitHub Release with an auto-generated changelog (grouped by `feat:` / `fix:` conventional-commit prefixes)
4. Auto-commits `Formula/{{.Name}}.rb` to the homebrew-tap repo via the GitHub API{{else}}`jwa-tobrew release` then:

1. Validates the working tree is clean
2. Tags `vX.Y.Z` (and pushes the tag over SSH)
3. Creates a GitHub Release with auto-generated changelog and uploads the artifact you passed
4. Computes the asset's sha256
5. Updates `Casks/{{.Name}}.rb` (or `Formula/{{.Name}}.rb`) in the tap repo
6. Commits and pushes the tap{{end}}

## Conventions

- **Conventional commits** (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`) — these drive the changelog grouping. `docs:` / `test:` / `chore:` are excluded from release notes.
- **Semver tags** with `v` prefix.
- The `--version` flag passed to `release.sh` is the bare version (`0.5.0`); the `v` is added automatically when tagging.

## When something goes wrong

- **"$GITHUB_TOKEN not set"** — you forgot the `op run --env-file=.env.template --` wrapper.
- **"working tree has uncommitted changes"** — commit or stash before releasing.
- **"tap origin is HTTPS but jwa-tobrew pushes over SSH only"** — the tap clone is misconfigured; switch with `git -C ~/developer/homebrew-tap remote set-url origin git@github.com:OWNER/REPO.git`.
- **goreleaser fails on dirty git** — same as above; the script requires a clean tree.
- **Sha256 mismatch on a fresh install** — re-run `jwa-tobrew bump {{.Name}}` from the tap; the asset was likely re-uploaded.

## What this skill is NOT

This skill explains how *this project* releases. It does not handle:

- 1Password setup or token rotation — that's `jwa-harden` (own repo)
- VPS deploys — that's `jwa-vps` (own repo)
- Anything other than cutting a new version
